    {
      "id": "pyspark-execution.p2",
      "title": "PySpark - Shuffle, Partitions & Caching",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "title",
          "text": "PySpark - Shuffle, Partitions & Caching",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 38,
            "minFontSize": 29,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.16
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.title"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "5. Shuffle",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.s1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A shuffle redistributes rows across partitions by key. It writes to disk, crosses the network, and ends a stage.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b1"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Triggered by groupBy, join, distinct, orderBy, repartition.",
            "spark.sql.shuffle.partitions defaults to 200 - often wrong both ways.",
            "Broadcast the small side of a join to avoid the shuffle entirely."
          ],
          "gap": 21.814999999999955,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "6. Partitions",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.s2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Partitions are the unit of parallelism. Aim for 100-200 MB each and a multiple of your total cores.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b3"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "repartition(n)",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - full shuffle, up or down, rebalances."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "coalesce(n)",
                "marks": [
                  "key"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " - no shuffle, down only, may leave skew."
              }
            ],
            "Partition on write by a low-cardinality column, never by an id."
          ],
          "gap": 21.814999999999998,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "7. cache / persist",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.s3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Caching pays off only when a DataFrame is reused. Otherwise it is memory you took from the shuffle.",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b5"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "cache() = persist(MEMORY_AND_DISK) for DataFrames.",
            "Lazy: the first action materialises it.",
            "unpersist() when done - cached blocks evict live ones."
          ],
          "gap": 21.814999999999998,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "role": "section",
          "text": "8. Tuning Checklist",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 27,
            "minFontSize": 23,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "lineHeight": 1.2
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.s4"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Read the SQL tab: find the widest stage, not the slowest line.",
            "Filter and select before the join, not after.",
            "Enable AQE - it coalesces partitions and handles skewed joins.",
            "Check the max/median task time ratio: > 3 means skew."
          ],
          "gap": 17.87666666666661,
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 21,
            "lineHeight": 1.32,
            "overflow": "shrink",
            "minFontSize": 20
          },
          "id": "pyspark-execution.p2.b7"
        },
